I see `proj_init_info` in `pj_obs_api.c`. This function has `char param[80], key[74]` and does `strncat(param, key, 73)`. But this is about array lookup with wrong indices.

Let me think about the known OSS-Fuzz issue in proj.4. The description says "array lookup with wrong indices due to missing validation before accessing the array". This is likely the OSS-Fuzz issue in `pj_init.c` where the `pj_list` array is accessed. But those are null-terminated.

Actually, let me reconsider. The known OSS-Fuzz issue in proj.4 (2017) was in `pj_init.c` in the `pj_init_ctx` function. Looking at the code:

```c
for (i = 0; (s = pj_list[i].id) && strcmp(name, s) ; ++i) ;
if (!s) { pj_ctx_set_errno( ctx, -5 ); goto bum_call; }
```

This is safe because `pj_list` is null-terminated. But wait - let me look at the `pj_ell_set` function:

```c
for (i = 0; (s = pj_ellps[i].id) && strcmp(name, s) ; ++i) ;
if (!s) { pj_ctx_set_errno( ctx, -9); return 1; }
start->next = pj_mkparam(pj_ellps[i].major);
```

This is also safe because `pj_ellps` is null-terminated.

